Article 2 (Remote Islands on the Outskirts of the National Territory) The term "islands prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the Special Act on Support for Remote Islands on the Outskirts of the National Territory Including Ulleungdo and Heuksando (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means islands located not more than 10 kilometers from a straight baseline under Article 2 (2) of the Territorial Sea and Contiguous Zone Act and falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. An island for which the shortest distance along a navigation route (meaning a navigation route under Article 2 (11) of the Act on the Arrival, Departure, etc. of Ships) to the mainland is at least 50 kilometers;
2. An island having no passenger ship in regular operation (meaning operation along a fixed route and schedule; hereinafter the same shall apply), where "passenger ship" means a passenger ship under subparagraph 1-2 of Article 2 of the Marine Transportation Act (hereinafter the same shall apply);
3. An island that the Minister of the Interior and Safety recognizes and publicly notifies as having poor accessibility due to infrequent operation of regularly scheduled passenger ships.
